# KNOWN idiom debt, one site per line. This file only ever
# SHRINKS: no tool path adds to it. A regex finding is fixed
# in the code or annotated `// LICENSED I<n>: reason` at the
# site. A `native:` finding carries no such comment (the rule
# reads none of its own) — it is fixed, or stays here, reviewed
# at adoption (avra-8sb5.25.16) and every time after. Most of
# the `native:` debt is STRUCTURAL, not owed: a rule's own
# quote pattern spells the shape it detects, so it fires on
# itself (compiler/idioms.av's own sites) or on the type's
# canonical identity comparison (core/nodes.av's `same_*`,
# already `// LICENSED I9` for the retired regex) — an
# irreducible base case, not a copy waiting to be centralized.
# `make idioms-accept` prunes what is gone. Burn it down.
